The rule for recover_json_object says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. For the input fence[ A S ] B, the fence holds A and S, so the last object inside the fence is S. For the rewritten text with one part added after the fence, fence[ A S ] B C, the fence still holds A and S, so the last object inside the fence remains S. Therefore the recovery answer is unchanged.